{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-30922" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}-5{e}^{-2x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059483/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e5564274dabab204427bc1c83433c24046ae11f9b03d346d205b81a5b55d1be"} {"question" "q-30922" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If we let $u=-2x,$ then,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-2\\,⟹\\,-\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u=\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nComputing our limits of integration, we get the following:\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\operatorname{ln}⁡4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡4$ |\n\nThen, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}-5{e}^{-2x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-5{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}{e}^{-2x}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-5{\\int }_{0}^{-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}{e}^{u}(-\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({4}^{-2})}{e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}({e}^{u}){|}_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({4}^{-2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}({e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({4}^{-2})}-{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}({4}^{-2}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}(\\frac{1}{16}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}\\cdot (-\\frac{15}{16}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{75}{32}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059483/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e5564274dabab204427bc1c83433c24046ae11f9b03d346d205b81a5b55d1be"} {"question" "q-30922" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059483/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c9f07aba1a0077a8905b623df6dbba39cd0d7940936c37291abb9dc09e69efbf"} {"question" "q-30922" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059483/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e5564274dabab204427bc1c83433c24046ae11f9b03d346d205b81a5b55d1be"} {"question" "q-30922" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{15}{16}"] ["math" "-\\frac{25}{16}"] ["math" "-\\frac{25}{8}"] ["math" "-\\frac{75}{16}"] ["math" "-\\frac{75}{32}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059483/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e5564274dabab204427bc1c83433c24046ae11f9b03d346d205b81a5b55d1be"} {"question" "q-30922" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{75}{32}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059483/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e5564274dabab204427bc1c83433c24046ae11f9b03d346d205b81a5b55d1be"} {"question" "q-30923" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{x/3}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059483/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e5564274dabab204427bc1c83433c24046ae11f9b03d346d205b81a5b55d1be"} {"question" "q-30923" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If we let $u=\\frac{x}{3},$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{3}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nComputing our limits of integration, we get the following:\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n\nThen, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{x/3}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{e}^{x/3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =({e}^{u}){|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & ={e}^{1}-{e}^{0} \\\\  & =e-1\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059483/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e5564274dabab204427bc1c83433c24046ae11f9b03d346d205b81a5b55d1be"} {"question" "q-30923" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059483/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c9f07aba1a0077a8905b623df6dbba39cd0d7940936c37291abb9dc09e69efbf"} {"question" "q-30923" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059483/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e5564274dabab204427bc1c83433c24046ae11f9b03d346d205b81a5b55d1be"} {"question" "q-30923" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{e}"] ["math" "e"] ["math" "e-1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059483/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e5564274dabab204427bc1c83433c24046ae11f9b03d346d205b81a5b55d1be"} {"question" "q-30923" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "e-1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059483/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e5564274dabab204427bc1c83433c24046ae11f9b03d346d205b81a5b55d1be"} {"question" "q-349595" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}4{e}^{5x}\\,\\text{d}x=$  \n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059483/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e5564274dabab204427bc1c83433c24046ae11f9b03d346d205b81a5b55d1be"} {"question" "q-349595" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If we let $u=5x,$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=5\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{5}\\text{d}u=\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nComputing our limits of integration, we get the following:\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\operatorname{ln}⁡2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $5\\operatorname{ln}⁡2$ |\n\nThen, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}4{e}^{5x}\\,\\text{d}x & =4{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{e}^{5x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{5\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{e}^{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({2}^{5})}{e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}\\cdot {e}^{u}\\,{|}_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({2}^{5})} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}({e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({2}^{5})}-{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}({2}^{5}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}(32-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}\\cdot 31 \\\\  & =\\frac{124}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059483/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e5564274dabab204427bc1c83433c24046ae11f9b03d346d205b81a5b55d1be"} {"question" "q-349595" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059483/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c9f07aba1a0077a8905b623df6dbba39cd0d7940936c37291abb9dc09e69efbf"} {"question" "q-349595" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059483/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e5564274dabab204427bc1c83433c24046ae11f9b03d346d205b81a5b55d1be"} {"question" "q-349595" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{124}{5}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059483/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e5564274dabab204427bc1c83433c24046ae11f9b03d346d205b81a5b55d1be"} {"question" "q-349626" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{3}3\\cdot {2}^{5-x}\\,\\text{d}x=$  \n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059483/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e5564274dabab204427bc1c83433c24046ae11f9b03d346d205b81a5b55d1be"} {"question" "q-349626" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If we let $u=5-x,$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-1\\,⟹\\,-\\,\\text{d}u=\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nComputing our limits of integration, we get the following:\n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $4$ | $2$ |\n\nThen, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{3}3\\cdot {2}^{5-x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{4}^{2}3\\cdot {2}^{u}(-1)\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-3{\\int }_{4}^{2}{2}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-3(\\frac{{2}^{u}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}){|}_{4}^{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}({2}^{2}-{2}^{4}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(4-16) \\\\  & =\\frac{36}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059483/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e5564274dabab204427bc1c83433c24046ae11f9b03d346d205b81a5b55d1be"} {"question" "q-349626" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059483/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c9f07aba1a0077a8905b623df6dbba39cd0d7940936c37291abb9dc09e69efbf"} {"question" "q-349626" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059483/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e5564274dabab204427bc1c83433c24046ae11f9b03d346d205b81a5b55d1be"} {"question" "q-349626" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{36}{\\ln(2)}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059483/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e5564274dabab204427bc1c83433c24046ae11f9b03d346d205b81a5b55d1be"} {"question" "q-349648" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-1}^{1}{3}^{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x=$  \n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059483/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e5564274dabab204427bc1c83433c24046ae11f9b03d346d205b81a5b55d1be"} {"question" "q-349648" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If we let $u=x+1,$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nComputing our limits of integration, we get the following:\n\n| $x$ | $-1$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $2$ |\n\nThen, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{3}^{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{3}^{u}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{{3}^{u}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\,{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}({3}^{2}-{3}^{0}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(9-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059483/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e5564274dabab204427bc1c83433c24046ae11f9b03d346d205b81a5b55d1be"} {"question" "q-349648" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059483/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c9f07aba1a0077a8905b623df6dbba39cd0d7940936c37291abb9dc09e69efbf"} {"question" "q-349648" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059483/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e5564274dabab204427bc1c83433c24046ae11f9b03d346d205b81a5b55d1be"} {"question" "q-349648" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{8}{\\ln(3)}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059483/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e5564274dabab204427bc1c83433c24046ae11f9b03d346d205b81a5b55d1be"}] "usage" {"q-30923" []} "basis" 1905 "retractions" [[17592186097136 :question/problem "What is $\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{3}e^{x/3}dx$?"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186095179 17592186095180 17592186095181 17592186095182 17592186095183] "immutable_fields" [[17592186095178 :answer-field/correct] [17592186095178 :answer-field/id] [17592186095178 :answer-field/key] [17592186095178 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
